//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// DATA LOADING CHECK
//
// This is an INDICATOR, not a strategy. No orders, no position, no sizing, no
// exits, no ta.* calls that carry state. It cannot be affected by anything in
// the trading logic. All it does is report what data TradingView actually gave
// the script.
//
// HOW TO USE
//   1. Add it to the same gold chart at the same timeframe.
//   2. Read the label at the right-hand edge.
//   3. Change to your other backtest range and read it again.
//
// WHAT IT MEANS
//   "bars loaded" or "first bar" DIFFER between the two ranges
//       -> TradingView is feeding the script different data. No script change
//          can fix this, and it fully explains why even a bare SMA crossover
//          gave different trades. Fix by enabling Deep Backtesting, or accept
//          that the chart cannot hold the history you are testing over.
//
//   Both IDENTICAL
//       -> the data is the same, so the difference is created by the strategy
//          engine (order fills, sizing, position carry-in), not the data, and
//          I will look there next.
//
// REFERENCE (what the full history should be, from the OANDA feed):
//       15m : 485,843 bars   from 2006-03-20
//       1H  : 122,765 bars   from 2006-03-19
//   A Premium chart typically loads ~20,000 bars, which at 15m is ~208 days.
// =============================================================================

indicator("Data loading check", overlay=true)

var int  barsLoaded = 0
var int  firstTime  = time
barsLoaded += 1

// Bars actually inside the last 365 days, for comparison against the total
var int  barsIn365 = 0
if time > timenow - 365 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000
    barsIn365 += 1

if barstate.islast
    txt = str.format(
       "symbol      {0}\ntimeframe   {1}\n\nbars loaded {2}\nfirst bar   {3}\nlast bar    {4}\nbars in 365d {5}",
       syminfo.tickerid,
       timeframe.period,
       str.tostring(barsLoaded),
       str.format_time(firstTime, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", syminfo.timezone),
       str.format_time(time,      "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", syminfo.timezone),
       str.tostring(barsIn365))
    label.new(bar_index, high, txt,
              style     = label.style_label_left,
              textalign = text.align_left,
              size      = size.normal,
              color     = color.new(color.blue, 85),
              textcolor = color.white)

// Also exported to the Data Window so you can diff two runs numerically
D = display.data_window
plot(barsLoaded, "bars_loaded", display=D)
plot(bar_index,  "bar_index",   display=D)
plot(barsIn365,  "bars_in_365d", display=D)
